{
 "_source": "src/game/rdplex.cpp:1461-2103 BuyUnit (tech-transfer block 1518-2100)",
 "_semantics": "Runs only on the FIRST purchase of a program (unit.Num == -1 and Cash >= InitCost; lines 1503-1516 - later unit buys return early). A single float accumulator tt starts at 0.0 (line 1518) and is NEVER reset between donor clauses within a target's case. Donor clauses are evaluated strictly in the source order listed under 'sources'. Two clause styles exist, recorded per source as 'mode': 'override' = `if (n > T) tt = (n-T)/D;` which REPLACES tt unconditionally (so a later donor can lower tt set by an earlier one - last matching donor wins, NOT max and NOT sum); 'max' = `if (n > T && (n-T)/D > tt) tt = (n-T)/D;` which replaces only when larger. Some clauses carry an extra 'condition' (`n > n1`, donor must exceed the first-slot program's current Safety). Caps are applied to tt at the exact point they appear ('cap' on a source = the `if (tt > cap) tt = cap;` executed immediately after that clause), so a cap also clips tt carried over from earlier donors, and a later, larger cap cannot re-raise an already-clipped value; 'cap': null means no cap statement follows that clause. The Nova/UR-700 case contains a literal `if (tt > 5.0f) tt = 20.0f;` which RAISES tt to 20 rather than capping (transcribed verbatim under 'expression'). Final assignment is `Safety = <literal base> + tt` where the base is a LITERAL IN CODE (not read from Equipment.Base), though every literal equals the program's data Base in urast.json for both nations; Safety is int16_t so the float is truncated toward zero (no rounding). Intermediate `Safety = 10 + tt` stores in the Atlas case (lines 1613, 1623) are dead stores overwritten at line 1641. 'fixed' overrides are evaluated AFTER the formula assignment and replace Safety unconditionally when their condition holds (an AND of two OR-groups, each `n >= 75`). Then `unit_ptr->Base = unit_ptr->Safety` (line 2100, int8_t), and VerifySafety (game_main.cpp:935) later clamps Safety >= Base, so the transferred value becomes a permanent floor. There is NO ownership test on donors: the code reads each donor's current Safety regardless of its Num. Because unowned programs load with Safety == Base (urast.json: probes 40, Atlas/Titan/Boosters 10, Saturn/Nova 5, capsules 5, LMs 10, Kicker-A/B 10, Kicker-C 5) and every clause threshold equals (or exceeds) the donor's base, an unowned donor contributes 0 - 'owned' effectively means 'Safety has been raised above its data Base'. The half-price sale (TurnOnly == 3) affects cost only. Misc donors are ROCKET slots 0 and 1, not Misc programs. Upstream array indices equal our slot numbers for all four groups.",
 "_divisor_note": "Divisors are float literals (e.g. 3.5f) and the numerator is cast to float, except the Titan/Proton guard `(n3 - 5) / 4.6 > tt` which is int/double. Where a guard divisor differs from the assignment divisor, both are given.",
